        "solution": "\u003cp>The form should accept Demo Ada plus 01234, preserve that raw code, and show the synthetic success status. Five Arabic-Indic digits fail this explicitly ASCII-only demo rule even though other systems may legitimately accept them. That is why the active repository's isWholeNumber predicate must be described separately. Whitespace-only names remain editable but fail eligibility. An invalid submission keeps the buffers and selects the first field needing repair.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For A🙂B, the UTF-16 representation has four code units: A, the emoji's surrogate pair, and B. Replacing location 1, length 2 with X yields AXB. Deleting a selected range uses the same helper with an empty replacement. A conversion failure returns nil; the caller must choose a safe no-edit or diagnostic policy rather than force-unwrapping it.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Provide localized labels and an error that names which rule failed. Keep the explicit Done path because submitLabel cannot supply a missing number-pad Return key. Test composition and selection through the real input method; a pure string helper cannot certify that experience. The report should identify the keyboard, OS, width, text category, and observed outcome, while marking unexecuted device fixtures pending. No live data or client submission is part of this exercise.\u003c/p>"
