        "solution": "\u003cp>A worked dependency audit places appearance restoration before bar construction because the delegate source states that bars snapshot appearance. It places account reconciliation before presenting an authenticated route, and schema migration before accessing a consumer requiring the migrated store. It puts a potentially deferrable telemetry operation in an unresolved category until its dependency and instrumentation needs are understood. The window callback and loading-view promise are separate boundaries.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The experiment sheet records revision, effective configuration, phone/OS, installation history, route fixture, process preparation, cache policy, and thermal condition. Row one is a terminated-process signed-out launch after a previous successful run. Row two is returning from background with process survival verified. Row three is a deep-link launch into a permitted synthetic destination. None is silently renamed “cold.” First frame comes from the supported launch metric; usable content ends at the defined readiness state and presented route; a follow-up interaction verifies that readiness has meaning.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For size, compare the same export/thinning report before and after a hypothetical dependency change, with executable, resources, frameworks, download, and installed figures separated. Leave all observations blank until execution. The recommendation is conditional: “Investigate the longest measured required startup phase; any deferral must preserve account and migration order and must pass first-interaction validation.” That is a concrete, reviewable design even before device access exists.\u003c/p>"
