        "solution": "\u003cp>The retained package exposes ZDModulesMocks with type dynamic; the sibling Project.swift declares it as a staticFramework. A sound report preserves both observations and identifies test consumers before recommending parity. It does not assume the same suffix or name produces identical packaging. For lottie-spm, record branch 4.1.3 and the resolution file's commit, not an invented exact-version requirement.\u003c/p>\u003cp>VendorCodec's contract names its consumer product, supported device and simulator variants, minimum OS, public interfaces, linked dependencies, resource bundles, privacy information, checksum, and origin evidence. License and vulnerability decisions remain pending until the selected artifact and its dependencies are reviewed. Module-version failure suggests interface/toolchain inspection; duplicate symbols suggest repeated definitions or linkage; a loader failure suggests embedding and run paths; a nil resource URL suggests bundle membership and lookup.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Reconstruction uses the prior manifest, relevant resolution file, source revision or binary checksum, generator and compiler versions, and unchanged resource inputs. A narrow source-package build can establish a compilation boundary, while an app or test-host build checks integration. Packaging and device execution require their own evidence. This is a worked review, not proof that either observed linkage route or the synthetic binary has been executed.\u003c/p>"
