        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Classify the first actionable diagnostic before changing the graph. A missing module suggests inspecting the consuming target's dependency, the exported product and module name, source membership, and supported platform. A UIKit import in a host-only test suggests the chosen platform is wrong for that test; use an appropriate iOS target and destination or keep the pure model test independent of UIKit.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Compilation without executed tests requires checking the test target's source glob, framework discovery conventions, and the selected scheme's test action. Listing a workspace verifies structure, not that it builds or runs. Keep the pure model lab on \u003ccode>swift test\u003c/code> for fast behavioral feedback and use Xcode for platform integration. Record the selected toolchain, target, configuration, and destination with results. Regenerating or changing signing without a related diagnostic can obscure the cause. A passing package test validates that package's behavior, not navigation, signing, or a full application.\u003c/p>",
