        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Make \u003ccode>load(draft:service:)\u003c/code> return a state enum. First guard that specialty exists; on failure, return the selection-required state before invoking the service. Inside \u003ccode>do/catch\u003c/code>, map every successful array, including an empty one, to loaded. Map known offline failure to retry guidance and keep unexpected failure deliberate. Missing procedure remains valid input rather than becoming a sentinel.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Use a deterministic fake configured with a result and a spy that records calls. A validation test should assert both the failure state and zero service calls; merely observing the message does not prove the ordering. Separate tests check independent draft edits, the empty-query display rule, empty success versus offline, and nonempty result preservation. Use Swift Testing or XCTest consistently within each test. These synchronous host tests establish the model boundary's behavior. They do not establish cancellation, localization, rendering, or any real network behavior that the lab does not implement.\u003c/p>",
