        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>MainActor isolates accesses to UI state, but an async method can suspend and let another operation change that state. Capture the current request revision when starting the load. After awaiting the service, check cancellation and confirm the captured revision still matches before assigning loaded. That protects against a service that finishes despite a cancellation request.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Perform the same freshness comparison in the catch path. Otherwise A's late error or cancellation can replace B's newer loaded result with failed or idle. Only the current request may apply the model's cancellation policy; this example chooses idle, while another feature could retain earlier content. Classify cancellation using the task state and the service's documented cancellation behavior rather than assuming every API throws the same error type. The async keyword does not guarantee off-main work, and actor isolation does not preserve pre-await assumptions. Use controlled A/B completions to verify both late success and late failure.\u003c/p>",
