        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>The outer modifier provides view-associated work and requests cancellation when its ID changes or its lifetime ends. The inner \u003ccode>Task\u003c/code> creates a separate unstructured task; it does not become a managed child merely because its code is nested there. Await the model's async operation directly inside the modifier so that it executes in the associated task instead.\u003c/p>\u003cp>If a synchronous event legitimately launches unstructured work, assign a feature owner, retain its handle, and cancel it at the defined stopping event. Dropping the handle is not cancellation, and weak capture only changes object ownership. Cancellation remains cooperative: check it after suspension and avoid mapping it to an ordinary unavailable error. Keep request revisions because old work may finish before or despite cancellation. Verify replacement and disappearance with a controlled service, including an old error after a new success. This reasoning defines a task and presentation contract, without asserting that a real transport stopped on a device.\u003c/p>",
