        "androidBridge": "An actor serializes isolated state access, whereas a Kotlin Mutex held across a suspend call can exclude other holders for the whole critical section. Swift actor methods permit interleaving at suspension; neither actors nor mutexes alone define account ownership, caller outcomes, or distributed transactions.",
