        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>A timeout does not prove that the booking failed on the server. Do not retry the write until the endpoint supplies a safe replay or reconciliation contract. If supported, retain one idempotency key for the logical booking across attempts; a new key per attempt defeats deduplication. Require a replayable body, an attempt cap, a total deadline, and cancellation-responsive delay. Decode or validation failures generally call for correction rather than repetition.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Assign refresh to the account service so concurrent failures can share one operation instead of causing a storm. Prevent refresh recursion, adapt credentials only at trusted HTTPS boundaries, and limit refresh attempts per request. Individual waiter cancellation need not cancel work needed by others; logout instead invalidates account generation and prevents stale refresh completion from restoring credentials. Distinguish authorization rejection from transient transport failure. Use synthetic tests for ambiguous write outcome, retry cap, delay cancellation, concurrent refresh, and logout during refresh before claiming the policy is implemented.\u003c/p>",
