        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Move resolution to a composition root and inject \u003ccode>any CardStore\u003c/code> with the feature's account context. Register the protocol type consumers actually resolve and fail visibly when required configuration is missing, rather than silently constructing a second fallback store. Choose and retain an account scope explicitly; a container-scoped instance may otherwise outlive the account it contains.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Provide isolation through the store's own mechanism, such as its actor, rather than assuming registration makes a mutable service Sendable. Logout must both clear stored account data and invalidate pending repository generations. Clearing alone allows an old request to write the previous account's data back. Verify A and B separation, clearing A without touching B, and a gated A load completed after logout. A child container also needs its intended owner to retain it. The memory implementation can prove these composition and lifecycle behaviors, while durable cleanup and protection still require adapter-level evidence.\u003c/p>",
