        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Account generation identifies an ownership period, not just an account string. Increment it on an account reset so the original A response remains stale after A-to-B-to-A. The request number answers a different question: which network load started most recently within the current ownership. Capture both before awaiting and validate cancellation, account ownership, and request freshness before committing synchronously.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Represent cached data as an optional snapshot. Nil means no successful snapshot exists; a snapshot with zero cards means a successful empty response and can be reused. Under the lab's policy, a cache hit starts no request and does not supersede an active refresh. A failed forced refresh throws but preserves the previous snapshot, allowing presentation to choose explicit stale-content behavior. The lab has no expiry or shared in-flight coalescing. Use gated fakes for reversed completions, account changes, empty cache hits, and failed refresh instead of assuming actor serialization proves the contract.\u003c/p>",
