        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Assign the composition owner to implementation selection and retain the account service's credential ownership. Route snapshotting captures one dispatcher for an in-flight request; drain-then-promote waits for active work before switching. Compare their complexity and shared-session lifetime requirements. Start with one read operation and preserve status handling, cancellation, headers, cookies, trust, interception, and tracing through injectable fixtures.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Require parity tests and controlled in-flight switching before a bounded rollout. Agree on outcome, duration, cancellation, refresh, and active-request measures with approved aggregate fields. Set cohort gates and stop conditions against comparable baseline conditions, leaving uncollected evidence explicitly pending. Recovery selects the old dispatcher for future requests according to the chosen switching policy. It must not automatically replay a timed-out write through another transport, because that can duplicate server effects. Name who pauses expansion and how retained old resources are released. Remove the alternate path only after stable evidence and owner review; a source review alone establishes no deployed migration.\u003c/p>",
