        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Assign the mapper owner to the stable-order contract and the feature owner to user-visible validation. Compare retaining scans for small inputs, set-backed membership while filtering the original input, and asynchronous scheduling if substantial CPU remains. The set candidate adds storage; a scheduling change adds cancellation, transfer, and presentation obligations. Recommend provisionally rather than treating complexity analysis as measured benefit.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Require full-output fixtures for empty, repeated, distinct, and order-sensitive inputs. Keep fixture construction outside mapping measurements and record representative sizes, release configuration, device conditions, samples, and memory. Then measure action to usable results, where network and rendering may dominate. Establish reviewed regression gates from observed variation and stage integration through an owned seam. If behavior or relevant budgets regress, stop expansion and select the previous implementation where the installed code supports it. Name the owner who reviews evidence and removes the old path. All uncollected measurements remain pending; no synthetic numbers become device results.\u003c/p>",
