        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>A thrown Swift Error travels through try and catch. A trap or invalid memory access requires crash evidence; a hang needs responsiveness and thread timelines; watchdog termination needs its reason and lifecycle context. Jetsam describes memory pressure and is not an ordinary crash backtrace awaiting symbolication. The slow request may be an operation failure without process termination, so its trace and outcome contract matter.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For the trap, retain the distributed archive and matching symbols for each relevant binary. A dSYM UUID must match the report's binary image; rebuilding the same source later can produce different identities and does not substitute for the original artifact. Inspect failure type, triggered thread, all relevant stacks, and cohort before choosing a hypothesis. Symbolication recovers names and lines, but a frame only shows execution at failure. Earlier memory corruption or an ordering bug can cause the final symptom. Record missing symbols and reproduction as diagnostic gaps rather than inventing a source-level cause.\u003c/p>",
