        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Define success as confirmed completion presented to the user, with eligible submission attempts as the denominator. Separate expected pre-submission cancellation from unresolved post-submission timeout; reconcile server state before replay. Assign crash-symbol investigation, memory investigation, and request tracing to appropriate client and service owners. Compare containment options: pause distribution, disable a compatible feature, restore a service contract, or prepare a corrective binary.\u003c/p>\u003cp>A pause does not repair installed code, and a flag cannot protect a failure before configuration is read. Require matching symbols, a supported mechanism hypothesis, and a regression test for the selected transition. Use allowlisted build, cohort, state, failure code, and bounded duration data, avoiding payloads and credentials. Recovery must compare confirmed-success and failure incidence for similar cohorts and windows, allowing for delayed or missing reports and sufficient volume. A lower crash count caused by abandonment is not recovery. Record who authorizes resumption, residual uncertainty, and artifact gaps; the scenario supplies no actual rates or diagnosed production cause.\u003c/p>",
