        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>The parent proposes dimensions, each child chooses a size, and the parent places the resulting children. A child need not accept an exact proposed size, and the parent can probe several times. An unspecified dimension asks about ideal size; zero asks about minimum behavior; infinity probes maximum behavior. Replacing nil with zero changes the question and can collapse content. A concrete reported size still needs a meaningful finite result.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For a finite column width, measure text with that width and sum the returned heights plus spacing between children. Place using a consistent width policy and the final bounds origin. A narrower multiline Text may become taller, so cached measurements must remain valid for the actual inputs. Empty children should not create a phantom gap. A vertical ScrollView commonly leaves the scrolling dimension unspecified rather than imposing viewport height. Define overflow behavior for children that exceed the budget. Layout methods can run repeatedly, so they are unsuitable lifecycle hooks for networking or state mutation. Verify different probes and final rendering separately.\u003c/p>",
